cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research artifact, please cite the archived Zenodo release once the DOI is registered."
title: "Measurement-Language Failure, Certificates, and Repair in Cellular Automata"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Earnhart"
    given-names: "Derek"
version: "0.3.1"
date-released: 2026-10-13
repository-code: "https://github.com/ImDerekEarnhart/representational-holes-research"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible research package for a bounded cellular-automata study of
  measurement-language failure, language-relative certificates, and prospective
  representation repair. The strongest result is the certified Rule 3/17
  translation-invariant language limit and a separately frozen parity-sensitive
  repair.
keywords:
  - executable observables
  - measurement languages
  - representational insufficiency
  - cellular automata
  - reproducibility
  - open science
